    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d601">

                <pb facs="0766" n="654" sameAs="frus:frus1918/pg654"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.516/209a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Mexico</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Fletcher</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-06-21T20:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 21, 1918, 8 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1192. Please forward by mail list of funds seized under decree of September 15,
                        1916,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d601-f1"/> from Bank of London and Mexico and
                    Banco Nacional, together with date of each seizure. Send similar information, if
                    available, with reference to all other banks of issue. Report also disposition
                    Mexican Government has made of such funds, especially those removed from banks
                    controlled by foreigners.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
